   "qtype": "numeric",
   "section": "Section B",
   "stem": "The length of the latus rectum and directrices of a hyperbola with eccentricity $e$ are 9 and $x = \\pm\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{3}}$, respectively. Let the line $y - \\sqrt{3}\\,x + \\sqrt{3} = 0$ touch this hyperbola at $(x_{0}, y_{0})$. If $m$ is the product of the focal distances of the point $(x_{0}, y_{0})$, then $4e^{2} + m$ is equal to ________.",
